"3168","Urwah reported: Aisha said: ""O son of my sister! The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) did not prefer any of us over another in the division of his time spent with us. Scarcely a day passed without him visiting all of us, drawing near to each woman without touching her until he reached the one whose turn it was, and he would spend the night with her. And Sawdah bint Zam'ah, when she grew old and feared that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) might separate from her, said: 'O Messenger of Allah! My day is for Aisha.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) accepted that from her. And concerning this, Allah the Exalted revealed [the verse], and in similar cases, I think he said: 'And if a woman fears from her husband ill-treatment or desertion...' (An-Nisa: 128)."
"3169",""
